{"title":"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(You_don&#39;t_remember_conic_section_formulae)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (You don't remember conic section formulae)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(No_Words)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (No Words)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that a parabola has vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/7/3a7dd52d57b27fe6dd1c7aeaa69e7eefb6233f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{4},-\\frac{9}{8}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" /> and equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878740b1e9bad0008122348eca48d8883a00e7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/5/d25634d7212302efdeb3702974863759bfb74d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer.  The minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be written in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the vertex is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/2/eb27d39322535f45618b24a4d3468bf0199ac5d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{1}{4}, -\\frac{9}{8}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"71\" height=\"43\" />, the equation of the parabola can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d6432df93f0e99fb3e99ae467b994c5879625c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=a\\left(x-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^2-\\frac{9}{8}.\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"46\" />\nExpanding, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/4/4940a8551305e9e18ec8dd7f2625326ad2efbf22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=a\\left(x^2-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{1}{16}\\right)-\\frac{9}{8},\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/238863a5cd45c31c4ae24d5341d585f90c4b889f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=ax^2-\\frac{ax}{2}+\\frac{a}{16}-\\frac{9}{8}.\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"37\" /> From the problem, we know that the parabola can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84cea4f7bfc5284747e737af0d1a25e64afdd47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=ax^2+bx+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer. From the above equation, we can conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/3/1a351eb298ff1526bb4bc134ed0a57e4a751b6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=a$\" width=\"43\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3aac744d48ce64da76d5cd115100d30ef5fb817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{a}{2}=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"33\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/b/85bf35819ac5ac15b5f92d10f8c30204967713dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{16}-\\frac{9}{8}=c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />. Adding up all of these gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/1/ea1d3cabd1e1c0ca4246c0b177abb321f1ea88bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{9a-18}{16}=a+b+c.\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" /> We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/e/cde5f0be6accc3395fab44438f5289205b69b9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9a-18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> must be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/3/f73a550a3bf6c460925ae7213c65ab99be501c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9a=z$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ff998e3f79f7b7fed7fc155b21ff50139c7117a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${z-18}\\equiv {0} \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/b/cab024624241abef2f5a2ddab525424f9b719423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${z}\\equiv {2} \\pmod{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/e/c5ebecd1b76f59d89c4bb0df8a3cc8006d42466f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9a=2$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee730e2c253c8e7fd057b55a9ec98ae16320db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />. Adding up gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d0f604bc1c8232af2694fd05af755d4a21ecd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+9=\\boxed{011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Complete the square. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, the parabola must be facing upwards. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/5/3d567c5b94ba695b493abdb5c57713d8886ae0f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=\\text{integer}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"144\" height=\"15\" /> means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> must be an integer. The function can be recasted into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/8/d18497177dc77c93c295e6b8c6854f44ac695d02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\left(x-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^2-\\frac{9}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"125\" height=\"46\" /> because the vertex determines the axis of symmetry and the critical value of the parabola. The least integer greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/310a8c4bfedf8ed0019b4b1489559496bbe60170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{9}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"37\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. So the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate must change by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db9e227e8177d26de452c2a2faeb6d45cc53d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate must change by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c29826428a8261b526c66746f4b59d9ab02b86c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9ed2cfaacd952677bdd8924f281df492eee8c11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)^2=\\frac{1}{8}\\implies \\frac{9a}{16}=\\frac{1}{8}\\implies a=\\frac{2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"301\" height=\"46\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/0/2d0f604bc1c8232af2694fd05af755d4a21ecd22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+9=\\boxed{011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To do this, we can use the formula for the minimum (or maximum) value of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> coordinate at a vertex of a parabola, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d743c434bc99610c1d2c89c318b57ecf38ab720c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"37\" /> and equate this to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3aac744d48ce64da76d5cd115100d30ef5fb817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{a}{2}=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"33\" />. Enter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d498e47847431c98fc06a9b684db142c1c62bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"38\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae2b515c0661582f6b08a9bf0217b4f46b2618f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{9}{8}=\\frac{a}{16}+\\frac{b}{4}+c=-\\frac{a}{16}+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"230\" height=\"38\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37400e5094a52b3ba0135d5c7a012e6b4f7a42f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{a-18}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a31f838d9b0cabb2e49408eb1e07d90f111747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9a-18}{16}\\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"99\" height=\"38\" /> so the minimum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is when the fraction equals -1, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/e/eee730e2c253c8e7fd057b55a9ec98ae16320db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{2}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d28f38ae8717c1136956cc5faad977fa9ce6893a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q=2+9=\\boxed{011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"23\" />.\n-Gideontz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4eca83231160ed52e066b84923ecbba25984c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\left( x- \\frac 14 \\right)^2 - \\frac 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"129\" height=\"48\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is equal to the value of this expression when you plug <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> in, we just need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b6271507ae90623ea3e917f17ec85d8c76b076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9a}{16}- \\frac 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" /> to be an integer. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, we also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/401dec816c8cfc36a30bca3535b7d1ee3960a2e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9a}{16}&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" /> which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/a/f0a17ab796e9636340152daf1abf70a140751f37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9a}{16}- \\frac 98 &gt; -\\frac{9}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"38\" />. The least possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is when this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa39587cd581ff35f15a7cc0e154fec2b667392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"49\" height=\"38\" />, which gives answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>-bobthegod78, krwang, Simplest14\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28You_don.27t_remember_conic_section_formulae.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(You_don't_remember_conic_section_formulae)\">Solution 5 (You don't remember conic section formulae)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (You don&#39;t remember conic section formulae)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take the derivative to get that the vertex is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/922971fd4dbfe177623db97a9b9dea5d60ba0d56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ax+b=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" /> and note that this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4686d88d9d482d91a3016b70f39f485c425017.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot a = -b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"84\" height=\"38\" /> and proceed with any of the solutions above.\n</p><p>~Dhillonr25\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96eb1b734debe94e4fe172fcfe3c8eab517a8288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Appendix to Solution 5 (You don&#39;t remember differential calculus)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"561\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Note that the quadratic formula for finding roots of parabolas is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd7e6a0d380937c33586961e28ff939d94dcd6f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"160\" height=\"40\" />, so if you average the two x-values of the roots the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c58a3c0d5156cb7fea9d064ee345a7ea24bb69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" /> part will cancel out and leave you with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/121cd605cf7dc1e301ccc7c17f9ad3cb39ca2c84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{b}{2a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />. Then proceed as above.\n</p><p>~WhatdoHumanitariansEat\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28No_Words.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(No_Words)\">Solution 6 (No Words)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (No Words)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878740b1e9bad0008122348eca48d8883a00e7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcb8f547eb44014771f96e3b48a1c3c16c18b62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a\\left(x^2+\\frac{b}{a}x\\right)+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"169\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d38bb20149473d572fed3e61b4b55be8280dc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a\\left(x^2+\\frac{b}{a}x+\\left(\\frac{b}{2a}\\right)^2\\right)-a\\left(\\frac{b}{2a}\\right)^2+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"340\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd58791792df57df04aa2f914a5be8bb352bf14b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a\\left(x+\\frac{b}{2a}\\right)^2-\\frac{b^2}{4a}+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"212\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6c85d930c98a58ca3a09734b9e229ee5c4cf51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b}{2a}=-\\frac{1}{4} \\implies b=-\\frac{1}{2}a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"194\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66cc8c9a804c85c141716396c699d8d19b9316e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- \\frac{b^2}{4a} + c= - \\frac{9}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/321c3eff7de3e9dbd7ef2d115bf26d88116eb989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\frac{b^2}{4a}- \\frac{9}{8} =\\frac{b}{2} \\cdot \\frac{b}{2a} - \\frac{9}{8} = -\\frac{b}{8}-\\frac{9}{8} = \\frac{a}{16}-\\frac{9}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"369\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f964d97a1fff8931ac4d3dc8be5f20a5edef355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=a-\\frac{1}{2}a+\\frac{a}{16}-\\frac{9}{8} = \\frac{16a-8a+a}{16}-\\frac{9}{8} = \\frac{9a-18}{16} \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"515\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed82734a68b126e1b288c5665e4fa7528e01157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\mid 9(a-2) \\implies a-2=b \\cdot \\frac{16}{9}, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"307\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f3b655d2c5d60d1d3d200eccc60bca44fcdad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{16b+18}{9} \\implies a = \\ldots, -\\frac{14}{9}, \\frac{2}{9}, \\frac{18}{9}, \\frac{34}{9}, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"369\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f51ad85d54dfe5bb727ee346d59d0fc0b6f8c8c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0 \\implies a_{min} = \\frac{2}{9} \\implies 2+9 = \\boxed{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"310\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vkniYGN45F4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vkniYGN45F4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I\" title=\"2011 AIME I\">2011 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•